            <ArticleTitle>Prinzmetal angina in the differential diagnosis of syncope.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/17482941.2011.655289</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prinzmetal (variant) angina may be associated with cardiac arrhythmias that can deteriorate to fatal ventricular arrhythmias. We present 2 patients with syncope where vasospastic angina and severe ventricular arrhythmias were found to be responsible for the syncopal episodes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
